 qemu-server (9.2.2) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * improve support for VMs running on the aarch64 (ARM) architecture:
     - honor the 'pre-enrolled-keys' setting of the EFI disk, which requires a
       pve-edk2-firmware-aarch64 newer than 4.2025.05-2 for the secure-boot
       enabled firmware image. Older versions keep the previous behavior and now
       log a warning pointing at the outdated firmware package.
     - recognize the EFI firmware pflash devices of QEMU's 'virt' machine, so
       that cloning a running VM with an EFI disk no longer fails
     - use the 'virtio-gpu-gl' display device, as QEMU provides only the non-VGA
